From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] diasymreader: SymWriter writes PDB files (3554)

diasymreader: SymWriter writes real PDB files

The symbol writer keeps documents (url, checksum, embedded source), methods with sequence points, scopes,
locals, parameters, constants and namespace usings, and on Close/Commit writes an MSF 7.00 PDB to the
file or IStream given to Initialize/Initialize2/IPdbWriter::SetPath: PDB info stream with GUID/age and
named stream map, empty TPI/IPI, DBI with one module, a /names table, a module stream with managed
procedure, block, slot, constant and namespace records plus C13 line and file checksum subsections.
State errors (no open method/scope/namespace) return E_UNEXPECTED, bad arguments E_INVALIDARG.
GetDebugInfo fills TimeDateStamp; Initialize2 records the final path; Abort drops the file.
